"guidance.manual.synologyDrive" = "Synology Drive has no settings export and its connection is registered on the NAS. Install the client, create the sync tasks again and point them at your existing local folders (it then only syncs changes); unlink the old Mac in the Drive Admin Console. MacReplica does not copy the client's database or session.";
"guidance.manual.calibrationSoftware" = "Display profiles are restored with the color profiles. Custom presets or workflows are stored inside the app: export them in the Preset Manager on the old Mac and import them on the new one. The licence is tied to the measuring instrument.";
"guidance.manual.benqPaletteMaster" = "The hardware calibration is stored in the monitor and stays there. Its ICC profiles come back with the color profiles and saved targets with the application data. With Palette Master Ultimate you can also use Account › Backup and Download.";
"guidance.manual.xppenDriver" = "Install the driver, then allow it in System Settings › Privacy & Security › Accessibility (XPPenDriver) and Screen Recording (XPPenTablet) and reopen it. The most reliable way to move the settings is the driver's own Export config / Import config (.pcfg). Set the screen mapping to the pen display and calibrate again.";
"guidance.manual.mailAccounts" = "Mail accounts and passwords are never copied. Add your accounts in System Settings › Internet Accounts (or Mail › Add Account) first, then MacReplica restores signatures and rules; check rules and smart mailboxes afterwards. With iCloud Drive for Mail they sync by themselves.";
"guidance.manual.officeActivation" = "Licences and sign-ins are never copied. Sign in to Microsoft 365 again, or – for a volume or perpetual licence – run the activation package you received with your licence again. MacReplica restores templates, AutoCorrect, dictionaries and startup files separately.";
