"sensitive.advice.passwordDatabase" = "Add it to the encrypted part of the backup: it comes back to the same place, checked byte for byte. You still need its master password – and its key file, if it uses one.";
"sensitive.advice.keePassKeyFile" = "Together with your master password it opens a KeePass database. Add it to the encrypted part of the backup, and keep another copy apart from the database (for example on another drive) so it stays a second factor.";
"sensitive.advice.privateKey" = "Add it to the encrypted part of the backup: it comes back to the same place, for your user only. If the key has a passphrase you need that too. Keys kept only in the keychain: export them in Keychain Access as a password-protected file.";
"sensitive.advice.certificate" = "Certificates are usually public. Add it to the encrypted part of the backup if you need it; it does not include its private key – preserve that as well.";
