"guided.source.choose" = "Choose a source …";
"guided.source.help" = "Where the app comes from on this Mac. Your own installer gives exactly the version you had, without the internet. The developer's update feed or download gives the newest version of the chosen channel (stable, beta …), which may need a newer macOS or change file formats. MacReplica suggests the source in the same channel as on the old Mac; it never switches a beta to stable or the other way round by itself. Homebrew always installs the current version of a package; older versions are not kept by Homebrew. An app that is already installed is never replaced or downgraded.";
"guided.source.noChannel" = "No source for the %1$@ channel you used was found. Choose a source yourself if you want to switch channel – MacReplica does not switch it for you.";
"match.help" = "MacReplica found several Homebrew packages that could install this app and is not sure enough to pick one by itself. Choose the one that is your app (name, package name and description are shown), or “None of these – install it myself” to install it yourself or with your own installer.";
"match.office.note" = "All these packages install the same Microsoft Office apps; your licence decides the edition (Microsoft 365, Office LTSC 2024/2021 or a retail licence). “BusinessPro” also installs Teams.";
"match.office.help" = "Microsoft uses one installer for Microsoft 365, Office LTSC 2024, Office LTSC 2021 and retail Office; the version number (for example 16.113) is the same for all. Choose the package for this app (e.g. “Microsoft Word”) or the whole suite (“Microsoft Office”). For Office LTSC 2024 the edition comes from your volume licence: after installing, run the licence package your organisation gave you (the Volume License Serializer). Add it with “Use my installer …” and tick “Contains a licence or activation”, so it is in the backup.";
"office.activation.volumeLicence" = "Office on this Mac has a volume licence (Office LTSC 2024 or 2021, or another licence for the whole Mac). The licence file is bound to this Mac and is never copied. On the new Mac: install Office, then run your Volume License Serializer package again (keep it with your installers). MacReplica cannot tell 2021 from 2024.";
"office.activation.signIn" = "Office on this Mac is activated by signing in (Microsoft 365, or a retail licence linked to your Microsoft account) – or not activated. On the new Mac: install Office, open Word and sign in. Nothing about the licence is copied.";
