"printer.section.help" = "macOS keeps the printers' setup in system files that only an administrator can read, and printer drivers are installed by their manufacturers. So MacReplica does not copy drivers or system files and never sets printers up by itself. It records what you need to add each printer again – name, connection, model, whether a manufacturer's driver is needed – and on the new Mac checks that each printer is there. Old drivers may not work on a newer macOS or on Apple silicon: get the current driver from the manufacturer. Print presets are not transferred.";
