"python.keepCopy.help" = "Normally an environment is rebuilt on the new Mac from its list of packages. A saved copy also keeps packages that cannot be downloaded again. It only helps when the same Python installation exists on the new Mac (for example when you reinstall macOS on this Mac); MacReplica runs the copy to check it and otherwise rebuilds the environment.";
"resume.help" = "A restore that was interrupted (or that waits for steps you do yourself) continues where it stopped: steps that are finished are not repeated, open steps are checked again. Review lets you change the selection first; Discard forgets the session – the backup and anything already restored stay as they are.";
"conflict.help" = "Keep this Mac's version: nothing is changed. Replace with backup: the backup's version is installed and the existing file is moved to ~/Library/Application Support/MacReplica/Replaced Files – it is not deleted. Keep both: the backup's file is installed next to it under a new name. Skip: this item is not restored. The suggestion for each item is the safe choice (for example the newer font version).";
"restore.dryRun.help" = "Shows what each step would do on this Mac – install, copy, keep, skip or wait for you – without changing anything. Use it before the real restore; the list can be exported.";
"selection.help" = "Saves which apps, data, folders, installers, settings and printers are switched on or off, and the backup location – no data and no passphrase. Next time MacReplica offers to use it; new apps and data that did not exist then keep their usual setting. A copy is saved next to every backup (MacReplica Selection.json).";
