"tools.gatekeeper.title" = "Gatekeeper and app security";
"tools.gatekeeper.summary" = "Shows whether macOS checks apps before they open, and helps you open one blocked app the way Apple intends.";
"tools.gatekeeper.help" = "Gatekeeper checks downloaded apps before their first launch: is the developer identified, did Apple check the app for malware (notarisation), and is it unchanged since signing? Approving one app (“Open Anyway” in Privacy & Security) lets only that app through. Turning Gatekeeper off for the whole Mac lets every app through, including harmful ones. Since macOS 15 that works only through System Settings or a configuration profile: at your request and after a warning, MacReplica prepares such a profile, you install it in Device Management, and MacReplica checks the result and helps you remove it again. If Gatekeeper is off on this Mac, this tool shows why and where you can turn it back on.";
"tools.gatekeeper.limit.global" = "MacReplica never turns Gatekeeper off by itself: it only prepares a profile when you ask, and you install it yourself in System Settings › General › Device Management. It only ever helps remove its own profile, never others. Since macOS 15, “spctl --global-disable” only reveals the “Anywhere” choice.";
"tools.gatekeeper.limit.quarantine" = "Whether one app is quarantined says nothing about Gatekeeper as a whole. Removing an app's quarantine mark skips Apple's malware check for that app; MacReplica does it only for the one app you chose, after a warning, and can put the exact mark back.";
"tools.gatekeeper.limit.hour" = "Apple shows “Open Anyway” for about an hour after macOS blocked the app, and asks for your login password.";
"tools.gatekeeper.limit.managed" = "On a Mac managed by an organisation, its settings win. MacReplica only shows them.";
