"tools.updates.title" = "macOS updates";
"tools.updates.summary" = "Stay on this macOS version and keep receiving its updates and security fixes.";
"tools.updates.help" = "An update (for example 26.6 → 26.7) improves the macOS version you have and fixes security problems. An upgrade (for example 26 → 27) installs a new major version. With “Install macOS updates” on, your Mac installs updates by itself; a new major version is installed only after you click “Upgrade”. MacReplica shows your switches, compares them with a setup that keeps you on this version and secure, and opens Software Update so you can change them (macOS asks for the administrator password); afterwards it reads them again. It never writes these switches itself and never turns off security updates. Where Apple still allows it (macOS 13–15.7.4 and 26), it can prepare a profile that postpones major upgrades by up to 90 days; you install it yourself in Device Management.";
"tools.updates.item.check" = "Check for updates";
"tools.updates.item.download" = "Download new updates when available";
