"tools.corners.title" = "Window corners";
"tools.corners.summary" = "Make app windows less rounded than macOS draws them. Experimental.";
"tools.corners.help" = "MacReplica writes an undocumented AppKit setting (NSConvolutionOverride1, and NSConvolutionOverride2 for utility panels) into your user's global preferences – the same as “defaults write -g”. Its value is the corner radius in points; macOS 27 uses 16 by default, macOS 15 used about 10. Apps read it when they start, so reopen them. It changes normal app windows, document windows, dialogs, sheets and alerts. It does not change Quick Look, menu-bar popovers, menus, Control Center, notifications or apps that draw their own frame. Apple does not document it; it works from macOS 26.4 and was tested on 27.0.1. A macOS update may change or end it. MacReplica keeps the previous value and restores exactly that.";
"tools.corners.unsupported.title" = "Not available on macOS %1$@";
"tools.corners.unsupported.message" = "The setting works from macOS 26.4. Earlier versions ignore it, so MacReplica shows no control here. macOS 15 and earlier already use smaller corners.";
