"tools.menus.title" = "Menus";
"tools.menus.help" = "macOS 26 and later draw menus as Liquid Glass with about 12 pt corners; the window-corner setting does not change them. A hidden AppKit switch (NSGlassMenusEnabled) brings back the older, non-glass menus with about 6 pt corners – a fixed style, not an adjustable radius, and the menu material changes too. It applies to context menus, pop-up menus and the menus of menu-bar items in AppKit apps after they are reopened. Undocumented: Apple may remove it with any update. MacReplica keeps the previous value and restores exactly that.";
"tools.corners.scope.classicMenus" = "Menus (classic style, ≈6 pt)";
"tools.quicklook.title" = "Quick Look and popovers";
"tools.quicklook.warning.title" = "Changing menus, popovers and Quick Look weakens your Mac";
"tools.quicklook.warning.message" = "No setting changes them. The only way is a plugin loaded into apps by a tweak loader (Plugin Playground), which needs System Integrity Protection partly off — debugging allowed (csrutil enable --without debug) — set by you in recoveryOS, and the loader enabled. That weakens your Mac's security while it is active. MacReplica's plugin does nothing on untested macOS builds and never loads into system UI processes, but a plugin loaded into apps can still make apps crash. Continue only if you accept that.";
