"guidance.credential.keychainPasswords" = "Not copied as a file. Best: turn on iCloud Keychain on both Macs (System Settings › your name › iCloud › Passwords). Or use Migration Assistant, or in the Passwords app choose File › Export All Passwords and import the file on the new Mac – that file is not encrypted, delete it right after importing. Certificates with their private key: export them in Keychain Access as a password-protected file.";
"guidance.credential.passkeys" = "Passkeys cannot be copied as files. Passkeys in iCloud Keychain come back when you sign in with the same Apple Account and turn on iCloud Keychain. Passkeys of a password manager come back with that manager’s sync. Passkeys on a hardware security key stay on that key – keep the key. A passkey stored only on this Mac (for example in a browser profile) is lost: add another sign-in method to those accounts first.";
"guidance.manual.passkeys" = "Passkeys cannot be copied as files. Passkeys in iCloud Keychain come back when you sign in with the same Apple Account and turn on iCloud Keychain. Passkeys of a password manager come back with that manager’s sync. Passkeys on a hardware security key stay on that key – keep the key. A passkey stored only on this Mac (for example in a browser profile) is lost: add another sign-in method to those accounts first.";
"guidance.credential.chromePasswords" = "Chrome encrypts saved passwords with a key in this Mac’s keychain, so copying its profile does not bring them back. Turn on sync with your Google Account, or export them (Google Password Manager › Settings › Export passwords) and import the file on the new Mac – then delete it, it is not encrypted. Passkeys saved only in the Chrome profile cannot be moved.";
"guidance.manual.chromePasswords" = "Chrome encrypts saved passwords with a key in this Mac’s keychain, so copying its profile does not bring them back. Turn on sync with your Google Account, or export them (Google Password Manager › Settings › Export passwords) and import the file on the new Mac – then delete it, it is not encrypted. Passkeys saved only in the Chrome profile cannot be moved.";
"guidance.credential.edgePasswords" = "Edge protects saved passwords with a key of this Mac. Use sync with your Microsoft account, or export them (Settings › Passwords › More › Export passwords) and import the file on the new Mac – Microsoft warns the file is not protected, delete it afterwards.";
"guidance.manual.edgePasswords" = "Edge protects saved passwords with a key of this Mac. Use sync with your Microsoft account, or export them (Settings › Passwords › More › Export passwords) and import the file on the new Mac – Microsoft warns the file is not protected, delete it afterwards.";
"guidance.credential.bravePasswords" = "Brave (built on Chromium) protects saved passwords with a key of this Mac. Use Brave Sync, or export them in Brave’s password settings and import the file on the new Mac – then delete it, it is not encrypted.";
"guidance.manual.bravePasswords" = "Brave (built on Chromium) protects saved passwords with a key of this Mac. Use Brave Sync, or export them in Brave’s password settings and import the file on the new Mac – then delete it, it is not encrypted.";
"guidance.credential.firefoxPasswords" = "Firefox keeps saved logins in its profile (logins.json together with key4.db). Use Firefox Sync, or export them (Passwords › ⋯ › Export Passwords; not encrypted, delete afterwards), or – with Firefox closed on both Macs – copy both files together into the new profile as Mozilla describes. If you use a Primary Password you need it on the new Mac.";
"guidance.manual.firefoxPasswords" = "Firefox keeps saved logins in its profile (logins.json together with key4.db). Use Firefox Sync, or export them (Passwords › ⋯ › Export Passwords; not encrypted, delete afterwards), or – with Firefox closed on both Macs – copy both files together into the new profile as Mozilla describes. If you use a Primary Password you need it on the new Mac.";
"guidance.credential.onePassword" = "Your vaults come back when you sign in on the new Mac – for that you need your account password and your Secret Key (in your Emergency Kit). Make sure you have the Emergency Kit before you erase this Mac. A 1PUX export is not encrypted; avoid it unless you need it.";
"guidance.credential.bitwarden" = "Your vault comes back when you sign in on the new Mac. If you want a file as well, use Bitwarden’s password-protected encrypted export – a plain .json or .csv export is not encrypted.";
