"sensitive.advice.recoveryMaterial" = "The way back into an account if you lose your second factor. Add it to the encrypted part of the backup, and keep a copy offline as well (printed or on another device).";
"credential.section.title" = "Passwords, keys and credentials";
"credential.section.message" = "Add any number of key files, password databases and other credential files – from any folder or drive. They are stored only encrypted, each checked after encrypting. Nothing here is in the backup unless you add it.";
"credential.section.help" = "Encryption: AES-256-GCM. A random key encrypts the files; it is protected by your passphrase (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256, 600,000 rounds) and by a recovery key MacReplica generates. Neither is stored. Each file is encrypted on its own, decrypted again and compared before the backup counts it as preserved. On the new Mac each file goes back where it was, with private permissions; an existing different file is never replaced without your decision. Keychains, passkeys and browser password stores cannot be moved as files – this section tells you how to move them.";
